Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 00:37:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00895/11171] [outer-loop] Outcome-verifier de-risk: learned
 process+self-consistency = 0.949 (the path)

Answers 'how to improve the verifier'. The fixed process-reward (fraction_certified) ranks
trace-OUTCOME at only 0.57 held-out -> why it failed as an RFT reward. Learning a multi-
feature outcome-verifier on GOLD: process-features-only = 0.739; +SELF-CONSISTENCY (majority-
answer agreement across the K samples, free during RFT) = 0.949 -> STRONG outcome certifier,
gate PASS. HONEST NUANCE: self-consistency alone = 0.927; the process-verifier adds only +0.02
-> headline is 'self-consistency teaches + small verifier boost', and the verifier's standalone
value is the CHEAP single-pass proxy for SC at inference + the cascade router (when to escalate
to a teacher). Caveat: gsm8k set 81% correct (high base rate). GREEN LIGHT for the improved-
reward RFT: weight traces by learned(process+SC) -> does 'verifier teaches' approach gold?
(after the 3-seed; fold in anti-rambling target-reformatting).

